{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1523800-starting-essence-plasm-etc","id":1523800,"title":"Starting Essence, Plasm, etc.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-07T17:44:14-07:00","id":1523800,"title":"Starting Essence, Plasm, etc.","content":"Vampires start with 1d10 vitae (+ applicable merits like Feeding Grounds), but I can't seem to find what other supernaturals start with. Is it the same, or do they start with different amounts? I would think supernaturals who have a harder time of gaining their particular resource (like demons with aether) would start with a lot less?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T18:40:05-07:00","id":1523804,"title":"","content":"Per their Character Creation Quick Reference sheets, werewolves start with 7 Essence, Prometheans start at half their maximum Pyros capacity rounded up, and demons start with Aether equal to their Cover. Per their character creation sections, mages and Sin-Eaters start with a full Mana/Plasm pool for their Gnosis/Synergy rating. Changeling doesn't specify starting Glamour and technically neither does Vampire (a Starting Vitae roll is a more generally applicable rule for when it hasn't been established how much Vitae a given character has), but Glamour is sufficiently easy to come by that you could basically pick any means of arbitration (half capacity plus Goblin Bounty dots would be my inclination). Mummy doesn't specify starting amounts but provides a number of means of getting it rather quickly or adjusting your effective capacity for Pillars; having any relics in your tomb's Lifeweb guarantees you at least one point at the start of each chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T03:24:22-07:00","id":1523812,"title":"","content":"In my copy of Changeling, the sheet at the back of the book has &quot;starting glamour=10&quot;, but as Satchel said, nowhere else is it mentioned by the looks. The sheet for Vampire likewise says a d10 roll, but the book doesn't seem to mention it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}